RACE: corrected LSM ledger, policy replay, and nine self-corrections

LEDGER (authoritative, reconciles exactly)
  1,802 account orders -> 303 LSM -> 277 filled / 26 never filled
  432 fills, 275 markets (258 in snapshot + 17 recovered, 0 unresolved)
  6,096 contracts, SUM OF EXCHANGE FILL P&L = +9.38 dollars
  0 unmatched fills, 0 duplicate fill_ids, 2 duplicate same-ticker orders
  elapsed time from the EXCHANGE created_time, not a local clock

VALIDATED
  - actual LSM P&L is +9.38, not the +143.38 previously published
  - the missing -134 is real settlement loss across 6 consecutive close
    windows (18:00-19:15): a sustained directional regime
  - those losers began filling in 0.4-15.9s; a 2s cancel recovers only 27.40,
    refuting the claim that RACE explains the giveback

MECHANISM SUPPORTED
  fill fraction by outcome (all 303 orders, unfilled = 0 percent):
    2s   winners 42.42 vs losers 38.29  (+4.1pp)
    full winners 87.68 vs losers 98.26  (-10.6pp)
  the 26 never-filled orders won 96.15 percent at the same average posted
  price as filled orders (69.58c vs 69.15c)

NOT ESTABLISHED
  close-window bootstrap over 7 seeds P(<=0) 0.053-0.064; moving-block
  bootstrap 0.059-0.072 at 30/60/90 min. No multiple-comparison correction for
  the ~15 policies examined. One close window carries 56 percent of the 2s
  effect. Adding 0.25s of cancel latency IMPROVES all policies, which a real
  monotone mechanism cannot do. The runner 5s loop cannot execute a 2s cancel.

NINE CORRECTIONS, every one of which had inflated a result:
  pooled strategies; 17 missing markets; microsecond timestamps; per-fill vs
  per-market; policy A dropping rank 3; fill fractions excluding never-filled;
  orders-table side inverted vs fills; rank on filled-only; single-seed p-value

